A||N||2||FieroAlex||My 86 GT wont start!!!||||4||
Z||000000||FieroAlex||04-17-2000||06:12 PM||||Hello Fellow Fiero Owners!<P>I got my 86 GT in September 1999. Its a silver, 4 speed, fully loaded but with no AC. I never saw the car running. It has been sitting for 2.5 years. The fuel pump was dead so me and a friend got together and changed it. the car still wont start. I have spark and 5 of the 6 spark plugs are new. Spark plug #6 (at the back near the air filter) is broken in there. I have fuel at the rail. Now when I crank the engine it seems like its not getting any fuel because after cranking it 4-5 times we took 2 of the plugs out and they were dry. I do have a very small fuel leak under the car. My friend looked it over and narowed it down to one of two things. the computer or the injectors. What do you guys think is wrong and what should I do?<BR>Thanks A lot!<BR>Alex<BR>86 GT<BR>MTL Fieros||||reg||4
Z||000001||stimpy||04-17-2000||08:19 PM||||A little lesson I learned from our friend George at the Fiero Shop in Hayward CA... check all your fuses. Sounds simple enough but a blown fuse in the ignition circuit crippled my dad's s/c 3.8 86 GT. That was a sad afternoon. Fortunately, we were at George's house and upon his advice we took a look and in minutes it fired up upon replacing a 20 cent fuse.<P>I'm sure Ogre and fieroshop (George) will have more learned advice for you, but if it's a fuse you just saved a bundle!<P>P.S. for God's sake, fix that fuel leak!! Too many Fieros have been sacrificed by flame already!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-17-2000||08:58 PM||||There is a fuse just for the injectors. If it sat for 2.5 years it could also be the fuel pressure regulator. If it had dried out and cracked (the diaphram inside) you may not have enough pressure.<BR>There is a port on the fuel rail to check pressure. It could also be leaking fuel there too! I've seen the regulators leak after they have sat dry for a while.||||reg||1
